Done on design/v1 after 0185015. Decisions: NoPrompt is a field on git.Repo and sync.Options, set only by the session-start hook; hand-run and session-end syncs keep prompts. WaitDelay is 2s on every git process; Go returns exec.ErrWaitDelay even when git exited 0, so run treats that as success with the output it has. Gotcha: a composite literal in an if header needs parentheses ((git.Repo{}).UserName). Untested: that the hook actually passes NoPrompt (no seam observes Options); the env test in internal/git covers the variable itself. UserName treats git exit 1 as unset.